{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"embattled-vast-crossbill","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nThe completion-verifier close gate cannot produce a verdict for a multi-criteria epic:\nthe PRIMARY agentic run — despite carrying the `record_criterion_verdict` tool, the\ncriterion-id manifest, and ~175KB of prefetched evidence (all child file_impact bodies) —\nissues a stream of reasonable `search_files` queries but NEVER calls\n`record_criterion_verdict`, cycling its query list until budget exhausts. Banking zero, the\nsuccessor-recovery also banks zero, and the deterministic zero-progress guard\n(`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:555`) fail-closes with\n`CompletionRecoveryError` (\"completion recovery banked no verdicts before exhausting its\nbudget\"). The close is blocked; only `--force` clears it.\n\nFirst observed closing epic cf3c-1444-863e-49d7 (4 ACs, graph=True, all 4 children\nclosed+certified).\n\n## Proven root cause (runtime-confirmed)\n\nInstrumented `CriterionBank.upsert` + per-run tool histograms across 3 live verifier runs on\ncf3c:\n\n- 1x budget (req_limit=24 / tc_limit=48): primary = 22 search_files + 12 read_file + 2\n  list_directory; successor = 18 search_files + ...; **bank upserts = 0**.\n- 4x budget (req_limit=100 / tc_limit=200): primary = **97** search_files + 12 read_file + 3\n  list_directory; **bank upserts = 0**.\n\nDiscriminating result: search_files calls scale with budget (22 -> 97) while banks stay 0.\n=> NOT a budget shortfall. The model treats banking as optional and defers to a final\nstructured emit it never reaches; it also cycles the SAME ~30 queries ~3x (a\ntermination-awareness failure the runaway-loop breaker misses because the repeats are\ninterspersed, so max_consecutive_repeat=1 / distinct_ratio_window=1.0).\n\nWiring verified correct (not the cause): the primary IS constructed with\n`extra_tools=[record_tool]` and `extra_context=<manifest>`\n(`completion_recovery.py:CompletionAgentStep.run`); `RunnerAgentStep.run` DOES forward both\ninto the RunRequest; `assemble_prefetch(graph=True)` DOES aggregate the subtree file_impact\n(all S3 test/impl/doc bodies) and `fit_within_ceiling` keeps all 119KB (model ceiling 2M).\nSo the model has the tool, the ids, and the evidence in-context — and still never banks.\n\nThe captured queries are reasonable (`require_s3_helper`, `heal_multi_bundle`, exact paths),\nso this is not a query-formulation bug; it is a banking-adherence + termination-awareness\nfailure.\n\n## Legitimacy: defect\n\nViolates a cited design invariant. `completion_verifier.md` §\"Incremental banking\" (lines\n~256-278) and the `completion_recovery.py` module docstring both intend the model to \"bank\neach criterion's verdict incrementally as it works ... if budget runs out mid-verification,\nonly the criteria you have ALREADY banked survive into recovery.\" Banking zero across a full\n(and 4x) budget directly violates that intent.\n\n## Taxonomy (LLM-surface)\n\nPrimarily #16 Instruction-locality (the banking directive lives in the prompt preamble,\nstructurally distant from the per-criterion search/read loop) compounded by #6\nTermination-awareness (re-runs the same tool cycle, cannot recognize \"enough to bank\").\n\n## Proposed resolution (KERNEL, affirmative-framed — to confirm via prompt-perturbation eval)\n\n1. Co-locate an affirmative per-criterion banking directive INTO the manifest that is already\n   appended per-run (`primary_criteria_manifest` / the extra_context seam), e.g.: \"For EACH id\n   below, gather evidence with at most N searches, then IMMEDIATELY call\n   record_criterion_verdict(id, met, evidence) before moving to the next id.\" This addresses\n   #16 (make the rule reachable at the loop point) and #6 (bound per-criterion search + force a\n   bank).\n2. (Optional, structural) For an epic whose every DIRECT child is closed AND certified and\n   whose file_impact_scope is `none` (child-delivered ACs), allow the child-closure evidence to\n   deterministically resolve child-delivered criteria without agentic re-verification —\n   extending the existing 6ec8 child-closure shortcut beyond \"every child is closed\" phrasing.\n\nFix must land under an LLM behavioral eval (pinned settings, multiple samples vs a predeclared\nthreshold, negative control) per the rebar-debug LLM-surface discipline; the RED artifact is\nthat eval failing on the current prompt and passing after the directive change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A behavioral eval reproduces zero-banking on a >=3-criterion graph=True epic with the\n      current prompt (RED), and passes (>=1 criterion banked, verdict produced) after the fix,\n      at a predeclared threshold over multiple samples.\n- [ ] The completion close gate produces a PASS/FAIL verdict (no CompletionRecoveryError) for a\n      multi-criteria epic whose children are closed+certified, without --force.\n- [ ] No regression on single-criterion task/bug close verdicts (existing gate tests green).","id":"0707-59ae-7db6-489b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Epic completion verifier banks zero verdicts, fail-closes multi-criteria epic close"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786250072988146001,"uuid":"11822dac-b54c-45b8-add3-c5248e2a0f21"}